{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ReebTowerJacobiAnger"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_on_growth_hyperbola","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_on_growth_hyperbola","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingJacobiAngerBridge.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**The binding growth tower lives on the `I_ν` hyperbola** (not the `J_ν` circle):\n`cosh²θ − sinh²θ = 1`. The binding-context restatement of `reeb_growth_hyperbola`; together with\n`binding_discriminant_nonneg` it places binding firmly on the growth side of the Jacobi–Anger\nbridge `I_ν(x) = i^{−ν} J_ν(i x)`, whose q-deformation is the Layer-2 q-Bessel kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_discriminant_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_discriminant_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingJacobiAngerBridge.lean#L60-L66","doc":"**Confinement: the binding discriminant is non-negative.** `τ² − 4 = 4 sinh²θ ≥ 0`, so the\nbinding kernel `x² − τx + 1` has real reciprocal roots `e^{±θ}` — a confined hyperbolic bound\nstate — for every real binding angle `θ`. This is the structural reason the cosh-form of `τ`\n(built from the bar-even gap `[2]_q`, `NaStokesKeystone`) describes a *bound* nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_discriminant_eq_four_sinh_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_discriminant_eq_four_sinh_sq","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingJacobiAngerBridge.lean#L53-L58","doc":"**The binding transfer discriminant is `4 sinh²θ`.** For `τ = 2 cosh θ`,\n`τ² − 4 = 4 cosh²θ − 4 = 4 sinh²θ` (via the growth hyperbola `cosh²θ − sinh²θ = 1`,\n`reeb_growth_hyperbola`). The discriminant of `R(q,x) = x² − τx + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_trace_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingJacobiAngerBridge.binding_trace_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingJacobiAngerBridge.lean#L46-L51","doc":"**Binding trace lies in the `|τ| ≥ 2` confined regime.** `τ = 2 cosh θ ≥ 2`, since\n`1 ≤ cosh θ` (`reeb_growth_one_le_cosh`). The depth-2 binding transfer is therefore always\nhyperbolic `SL₂(ℝ)` (a real binding angle `θ` exists), never elliptic. ","signatureChunk":0}]}